User POV: two audiences — API consumers of the FastAPI backend, and end users of the shipped Expo/React Native app (web bundle on Cloudflare Pages plus native builds). Those are the product.
"User-facing" = something an API client or a shipped-app user can observe. Root dev tooling is not user-facing.

# Only deltas from git-ai's default type heuristics:
- Behavior change under fastapi/ (endpoints, schemas, auth, validation, ranking) → feat when it adds capability, fix when it corrects existing behavior
- frontend/ screen, navigation, or visible UX change → feat (fix when correcting broken behavior)
- Root dev tooling only (lefthook.yml, mise.toml, Makefile, scripts/, docs/src, .github/workflows) with no runtime behavior change → chore, or ci/build for pipeline and build-system edits — never feat
- Restructuring with no observable behavior change in either package → refactor
- Release plumbing only (version.txt, CHANGELOG.md, .release-please-manifest.json) → chore
